<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18529" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφρόνιτρον</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφρόλιτρον</span></b>  (the two distd. by
		Gal.l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
			<u>Gp.</u>
			2.28
		</span></i>), τό, a form of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>native sodium carbonate</i> (cf.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νίτρον</span>), distd. by <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.212
			</span></i> from the finer <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθος
			νίτρου,</span> cf. <i><span class="en">
				Herod.Med.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				6.20.5
			</span></i>: in <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i> and correct Greek divisim <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφρὸς
				νίτρου</span>: hence <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφρόνιτρον</span> is condemned by <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				272
			</span></i>.</div>
